.TH MD_PIN_FREQUENCY 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_pin_frequency \- select and pin a channel at a requested frequency
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_pin_frequency(morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, float hz);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select and pin a channel at a requested frequency.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I hz
Finite requested Hz. I/Q accepts negative, zero and positive IF offsets; audio
accepts zero and positive frequencies.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder, non-finite hz, negative audio frequency, or a flushed handle.
.TP
.B ENOSPC
A new tracking slot is needed but all slots are occupied.
.SH REMARKS
Rounds to a spectrum bin and clamps to the usable interval, leaving ten
retained bins on either edge as tracking guards. Reuses a channel within two
bins of the requested bin if available, otherwise creates one. It releases any
previous current pin, selects the channel, and prevents its automatic
retirement and automatic current-channel switching. Other channels continue to
be discovered and processed.
.PP
The channel still tracks pitch; pinning does not fix the exact measured
frequency, alter FFT geometry, or tune the input. A zero request can only
select 0 Hz if the configured retained band and its guards include that bin.
Requests outside the usable band are clamped, not rejected. Query
md_get_frequency() or md_get_channel() for the actual result.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_set_frequency (3),
.BR md_unpin_frequency (3),
.BR md_get_frequency (3),
.BR md_get_geometry (3)
